@startuml toolkit-node-disk-layout
title Node disk layout — catalog per network + saved paths

skinparam shadowing false

file "networks/tron.yml\ndiskRoles: fullnode, solidity" as TronYml
file "networks/bitcoin.yml\ndiskRoles: blockchain, index" as BtcYml
file "networks/solana.yml\ndiskRoles: ledger, accounts, snapshots" as SolYml

component "GET /api/host/disks" as HostDisksRoute
component "GET /api/nodes/{id}/disk-layout" as DiskLayoutRoute
component "GetHostDisksUseCase" as HostDisksUC
component "GetNodeDiskLayoutUseCase" as DiskLayoutUC
component "NetworkDiskLayoutCatalog" as Catalog
database "nodes.disk_layout_json" as NodeDb
component "HttpHostDiskReader\n→ agent GET /api/v1/host/disks" as AgentReader

TronYml --> Catalog
BtcYml --> Catalog
SolYml --> Catalog

HostDisksRoute --> HostDisksUC
HostDisksUC --> Catalog
HostDisksUC --> AgentReader
HostDisksUC --> HostDisksRoute : disks, mounts,\nsummary

DiskLayoutRoute --> DiskLayoutUC
DiskLayoutUC --> NodeDb : read saved layout
DiskLayoutUC --> Catalog : multi_disk_roles,\nlayout_rules
DiskLayoutUC --> HostDisksUC : host inventory\n→ recommended
DiskLayoutUC --> DiskLayoutRoute : disk_layout.roles[]\n(id, label, mount, dir)

note right of Catalog
  Each network defines JBOD roles
  (what to store where). Env sizing
  from diskHintGiB / fullNodeGiB.
end note

note bottom of DiskLayoutRoute
  Solana: ledger / accounts / snapshots
  TRON: fullnode / solidity
  Bitcoin: blockchain / index
  Operator picks mount per role on Disks step;
  PUT persists JSON to nodes row.
end note

@enduml


